01:03:31,764 --> 01:03:37,764
Antitrust (also titled Conspiracy.com and Startup) is a 2001 American
techno-thriller film directed by Peter Howitt and written by Howard Franklin.

11
01:09:52,941 --> 01:09:58,941
The film stars Ryan Phillippe, Rachael Leigh Cook,
Claire Forlani and Tim Robbins.

12
01:16:14,117 --> 01:16:20,117
It portrays young idealistic programmers and a large corporation (NURV) that offers a significant salary, an informal
working environment, and creative opportunities for those talented individuals willing to work for them.

13
01:22:35,294 --> 01:22:41,294
The charismatic CEO of NURV seems to be good-natured, but new employee Milo Hoffman
begins to unravel the terrible hidden truth of NURV's operation.

14
01:28:56,470 --> 01:29:02,470
Antitrust opened in the United States on January 12, 2001 to generally negative reviews from critics,
and was a box office failure, grossing $18 million against a budget of $30 million.

15
01:35:17,647 --> 01:35:23,647
The film explores themes of computer, hacker, technology, minidisc, garage.

16
01:41:38,823 --> 01:41:44,823
The tone is emotional.
